{
  "//": "K-01's measurement passage (docs/bundled-voice-plan.md §6, K-01). ONE passage, shared by the on-phone probe (K-01) and the founder audition (K-03), so the thing Wyatt and Joey rank is the thing the probe timed. Four lines, 1,315 characters, 77.4 s at narration-craft.md §2a's 17 characters/second planning rate — the deck says ≈ 90 s, and this is the real count rather than the estimate. It is long enough for the measurement it has to support (a warm RTF over three lines after a cold first one) and short enough that a founder will actually sit through it twice.",
  "//shape": "Every line carries `id`, `kind`, `text`, `chars`, `est_sec`, `phonemes` and `ids`. `phonemes` is misaki en-US IPA with the lexicon applied first; `ids` is what the Kokoro ONNX graph actually eats — the phoneme string mapped character-by-character through tools/narration/kokoro-vocab.json (the pinned export's own tokenizer table), wrapped in the pad id at both ends. FILLED 2026-09-12 by running `python tools/narration/phonemize.py --passage tools/mobile/kokoro-probe-passage.json --in-place` on a machine with misaki[en]==0.9.4 and its espeak-ng fallback installed; re-running it produces a byte-identical file, which is K-02's stated acceptance. Nothing here was hand-written: the ids were never typed, and a phoneme with no id in the table is a refusal in `ids_for`, not a silent skip, because a dropped character would both mispronounce the word and shift the style-vector row the whole line is sung with.",
  "//inert": "The probe is no longer inert on the passage's account: `player/kokoro-probe.js`'s `passageProblem` now returns null for this file, which is what turns the founder's `could not measure: passage-unphonemized` into a run. The two things that still have to be true on the phone are the bundled weights (`model-absent` if the build skipped tools/mobile/fetch-models.mjs) and a registered runtime (`engine-absent`). Nothing about how narration is spoken today reads this file.",
  "//espeak": "`espeak_fallback` per line, and `espeak_fallback_terms` at the top, are the words misaki's dictionary did not have and espeak-ng guessed at (misaki rating < 4). READ THIS BEFORE JUDGING PRONUNCIATION: five of the six terms in `lexicon_terms` are in that list, because 82 of the lexicon's 83 `ipa` fields are still null and there is therefore nothing to override them with. For K-01 that is harmless — it measures speed, memory and whether synthesis survives the lock screen, and espeak's guess takes exactly as long to sing as the right answer. For K-03's audition it is NOT harmless: the fixture line cannot be evidence about pronunciation control until those `ipa` fields are authored. That is a human job and it is not done.",
  "//lexicon": "The fixture line carries exactly six terms from mobile/plugins/foray-tts/lexicon/hard-terms.json, listed in `lexicon_terms`. They are the six the probe and the audition are both judged on: a voice that mangles them is not shippable however fast it renders.",
