      "id": "probe-02-beat-fire",
      "kind": "narration",
      "text": "Barbecue is a trade: it turns cheap, tough protein into abundance using fire, smoke and hours instead of cash. Follow the fire and you get technique — combustion, collagen, the chemistry of smoke, the difference between a skewer over coals and a pit dug into the ground. The traditions resemble each other because they are independent answers to the same physics, and the local variables are fuel, animal and faith.",
