      "id": "probe-03-beat-labour",
      "kind": "narration",
      "text": "Follow the labour instead and you get history. Because the hours are long, barbecue cannot be one person's weekday dinner; it needs a crowd, so it becomes an institution. And because those hours are hot and punishing, every barbecue culture has to answer the question of who tends the fire — which is always, underneath, a question about who holds power and who gets the credit.",
