      "id": "probe-04-lexicon-fixture",
      "kind": "fixture",
      "text": "Six names the narrator has to get right. In Japan the charcoal is binchōtan. In Yucatán the pit is a barbacoa. On the Argentine parrilla it is an asado, and in South Africa the same fire is a braai. The Quechua word for dried, salted meat is ch'arki, and the Taíno of the Caribbean gave the technique the word we still use.",
